ence, even some of those historical identities were recorded as Heroic Spirits in the Throne of Heroes to Mercurius’s amazement . Eventually, after an innumerable recurring histories, Mercurius visually knew everything in the world because he already experienced it repeatedly and all other all possible alternatives in all of creationbecause he has seen so much that ordinary surprises, eras, ambitions, tragedies, victories, mysteries, human struggles, even endless histories, parallel worlds, divergences, have largely lost their novelty and eventually he even lost interest in the Root not because he knew everything about the Root, because the give no meaning to his objective despite his close proximity to it, leaving him afflicted by an immense existential boredom and weariness beneath his playful exterior, which is why Mercurius strives to achieve the unknown, not because he wants to learn all things anymore, but because he is hopelessly bored. Only until the existence of Void Shiki and her Origin of Nothingness created a direct connection to the Root, which was something “unknown” to Mercurius and begins to fall in love with her, which alter his desire for the unknown by dying in her arms as his accepted conclusion.

